WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:02.890
Lord Van!

00:02.890 --> 00:04.480
Please wake up.

00:05.420 --> 00:07.110
What's the matter?

00:07.110 --> 00:08.990
It's still early.

00:09.280 --> 00:10.570
It's urgent!

00:10.570 --> 00:13.990
Sir Dee and Sir Esparda 
are already hurrying to the site.

00:14.330 --> 00:15.570
The site?

00:15.570 --> 00:19.620
The lake you created behind 
the village the other day.

00:19.900 --> 00:21.120
Lake Van.

00:21.120 --> 00:21.930
Huh?

00:23.770 --> 00:27.320
Wait, "Lake Van"? 
How'd it get that name?

00:27.690 --> 00:32.430
The villagers named it that to honor 
your deeds for generations to come.

00:32.430 --> 00:36.210
By the way, they're thinking what 
to call the village, and Van Village—

00:35.400 --> 00:36.210
Stop.

00:36.210 --> 00:38.120
That sounds all kinds of bad.

00:39.570 --> 00:41.350
Our lord has arrived.

00:41.350 --> 00:42.270
Lord Van.

00:42.270 --> 00:43.810
What is it?

00:43.810 --> 00:44.860
Well...

00:46.570 --> 00:48.450
Huh? What the...

01:01.370 --> 01:06.550
EASYGOING TERRITORY DEFENSE
BY THE OPTIMISTIC LORD

01:06.550 --> 01:09.130
EPISODE 5: A RARE SPECIES' 
PASSIONATE ENGAGEMENT COMPETITION

02:22.490 --> 02:28.750
EPISODE 5: A RARE SPECIES' 
PASSIONATE ENGAGEMENT COMPETITION

02:22.710 --> 02:26.450
She's an apkallu. 
They are half-human, half-fish.

02:26.450 --> 02:27.840
An apkallu?

02:27.840 --> 02:28.750
Yes.

02:29.290 --> 02:32.890
They're reputed to live in 
picturesque rivers in deep forests,

02:32.890 --> 02:36.230
but for some reason, a number 
are here in this lake you made.

02:37.020 --> 02:40.800
They're a rare species 
that few ever encounter.

02:41.160 --> 02:42.940
I see.

02:42.940 --> 02:46.520
Um, excuse me. Did you need something?

02:48.620 --> 02:51.210
Uh... What's your name?

02:52.970 --> 02:55.140
Can she understand what I'm saying?

02:55.530 --> 02:58.410
Till, Khamsin, could you bring some meat?

02:58.410 --> 02:59.530
Sure.

03:01.930 --> 03:03.740
Have some if you like.

03:03.980 --> 03:07.120
<i>Offering food is a good way 
to demonstrate friendship.</i>

03:11.170 --> 03:12.070
Here she comes.

03:20.710 --> 03:22.050
I can eat this?

03:22.610 --> 03:23.350
Yeah.

03:27.830 --> 03:29.180
This meat...

03:29.620 --> 03:32.100
It's armored lizard meat.

03:32.100 --> 03:35.190
If you'd like more tomorrow, 
I can make some jerky.

03:35.610 --> 03:37.940
Who defeated the armored lizards?

03:37.940 --> 03:39.690
Oh, that would be—

03:39.690 --> 03:40.770
Lord Van did.

03:40.770 --> 03:42.570
Lord Van's strength made it happen.

03:42.570 --> 03:44.170
It was Lord Van!

03:44.170 --> 03:46.700
No, no, it was thanks to all of you.

03:47.560 --> 03:48.420
I see.

03:51.330 --> 03:52.860
What was that about?

03:53.190 --> 03:54.830
Think she'll be back?

03:54.830 --> 03:59.510
Their species is rarely sighted. 
She likely won't return for some time.

04:00.840 --> 04:02.540
Stands to reason.

04:03.590 --> 04:05.840
THE NEXT DAY

04:09.350 --> 04:11.100
What is this?

04:11.490 --> 04:13.220
Oh, it's that girl.

04:13.220 --> 04:17.970
You're right. The one who asked us
who'd defeated the armored lizards.

04:18.790 --> 04:23.390
The apkallu don't view armored lizards
 as gods or something, do they?

04:23.390 --> 04:26.620
I've never heard of such a belief.

04:26.620 --> 04:27.740
Then...

04:30.770 --> 04:34.250
I would like to speak with the young man.

04:34.750 --> 04:36.360
S-Sure.

04:36.770 --> 04:39.610
<i>That's one scary look. What does he want?</i>

04:40.090 --> 04:41.880
Thank you for being kind to my daughter.

04:41.880 --> 04:43.680
Your daughter?

04:43.680 --> 04:45.190
Oh, you mean...

04:45.880 --> 04:50.140
Young man, I hear you're the one 
who defeated the armored lizards.

04:50.580 --> 04:53.890
It appears that's what 
everyone has agreed on.

04:54.120 --> 04:54.980
No way!

04:54.980 --> 04:56.120
This young child?

04:55.540 --> 04:57.400
You're kidding!

04:56.120 --> 04:57.400
Is he a powerful mage?

04:57.400 --> 04:59.490
Although I didn't defeat them on my <i>own</i>—

04:59.490 --> 05:01.720
Hero, you have my permission.

05:02.050 --> 05:05.990
You may marry my daughter, Lada Priora.

05:05.990 --> 05:06.910
Huh?

05:07.580 --> 05:09.100
M-Marry?!

05:09.870 --> 05:12.030
Does the arrangement dissatisfy you?

05:12.030 --> 05:16.030
I am Ladavesta, and Lada Priora 
is my only daughter.

05:16.030 --> 05:20.500
When she grows up, her beauty will
 shine as bright as any precious gem.

05:20.830 --> 05:22.150
But...

05:23.210 --> 05:26.220
Lada Priora is still a child.

05:26.220 --> 05:29.090
I don't think she understands 
what you're suggesting.

05:30.360 --> 05:34.870
Why <i>are</i> you offering her hand in marriage?
Is there a reason behind it?

05:36.020 --> 05:41.110
Until now, my people have 
avoided making ties with humans,

05:41.630 --> 05:46.810
but in recent years, armored lizards 
have encroached on our rivers,

05:46.810 --> 05:48.940
and many of our number have been lost.

05:49.860 --> 05:54.320
That is why I seek someone strong
to become Lada Priora's husband.

05:54.320 --> 05:57.660
I wish to secure a place 
for us to live in peace.

05:58.230 --> 06:01.460
<i>In other words, he's offering up
his daughter as a bride</i>

06:01.460 --> 06:04.270
<i>in order to forge an alliance 
with a powerful human.</i>

06:05.110 --> 06:08.580
In that case, the marriage
 part is unnecessary.

06:09.020 --> 06:12.680
Please allow your daughter to marry 
whomever she chooses in the future.

06:13.380 --> 06:14.680
You're refusing?

06:14.680 --> 06:19.060
I'll protect your tribe, 
regardless of any marriage.

06:19.690 --> 06:21.810
You sincerely mean that?

06:22.060 --> 06:23.440
Of course.

06:24.890 --> 06:27.820
Then, we shall settle here.

06:28.210 --> 06:31.490
Well, since that's settled, 
let's get building.

06:35.620 --> 06:37.960
What incredible magic.

06:37.960 --> 06:41.490
It's a rest area. 
Everyone can use it at their leisure.

06:41.490 --> 06:44.790
It's very spacious and seems 
like a nice, relaxing place.

06:44.790 --> 06:47.590
You'll be safe in here even 
when it's gusty and rainy.

06:54.970 --> 06:57.080
I'm glad everyone's enjoying themselves.

06:57.080 --> 07:00.220
Lord Van. It's nearly time
 to deal with the sewage.

07:00.220 --> 07:01.980
Oh, that's right.

07:01.980 --> 07:03.720
What are you going to do?

07:03.720 --> 07:07.860
Well, you see, I've placed sewer pipes 
underneath the buildings in the village.

07:08.260 --> 07:12.380
We regularly send water from the moat 
down them to flush away all the sewage.

07:12.380 --> 07:14.870
Otherwise, it'd get unsanitary.

07:15.140 --> 07:18.160
I see. Then, let us help you.

07:18.160 --> 07:19.750
Huh? You don't mind?

07:20.050 --> 07:22.830
We excel at working in the water.

07:22.830 --> 07:24.750
Thank you so much.

07:27.010 --> 07:28.510
Okay, we're opening it now.

07:36.630 --> 07:39.020
That went well, thanks to your help.

07:39.540 --> 07:42.130
Do you do that every day?

07:42.130 --> 07:44.330
Yes. Several times a day, in fact.

07:44.330 --> 07:45.520
I see.

07:45.820 --> 07:49.030
Then, allow us to take on the task
 of handling this "sewage."

07:49.030 --> 07:50.420
You mean it?

07:50.420 --> 07:52.930
Consider it thanks
for letting us live here.

07:52.930 --> 07:54.690
That'd be a huge help.

07:54.690 --> 07:56.520
Oh, Lord Van.

07:57.390 --> 07:59.010
There you are.

07:59.010 --> 07:59.910
What are you up—

08:00.340 --> 08:02.670
What? Those are apkallu!

08:02.670 --> 08:04.540
I've never seen one before.

08:04.890 --> 08:09.050
Son-in-law, you have my gratitude 
for your kind welcome.

08:09.050 --> 08:10.920
S-Son-in-law?

08:10.920 --> 08:13.500
Surely not. You married an apkallu?

08:13.500 --> 08:14.930
Uh, no, I haven't—

08:14.930 --> 08:16.980
Yup, I'm Van's wife.

08:16.980 --> 08:18.310
Van is my husband.

08:18.310 --> 08:20.020
Lada Priora?!

08:20.020 --> 08:22.390
See you later, husband.

08:29.780 --> 08:32.630
Lady Arte, sorry for calling you
 out here so early.

08:33.140 --> 08:37.350
I just thought it might be nice 
to take in the morning air on the lake.

08:37.350 --> 08:43.160
I-It's fine. I like taking in the 
morning air, too. It's very refreshing.

08:43.450 --> 08:45.100
I'm glad to hear it.

08:45.530 --> 08:49.310
Um, about that apkallu from yesterday...

08:49.310 --> 08:51.670
I heard the story from Panamera.

08:51.990 --> 08:55.180
It sounds like we both misunderstood.

08:55.180 --> 08:56.990
Th-That's right.

08:56.990 --> 09:00.420
I'm sorry for jumping to conclusions.

09:00.420 --> 09:02.070
I'm happy that's ironed out.

09:03.790 --> 09:09.310
You built this lake and developed 
the village so much. You're incredible.

09:09.750 --> 09:13.570
Not at all. It was all thanks 
to everyone else helping me.

09:16.120 --> 09:17.820
Good morning, husband.

09:17.820 --> 09:19.610
Lada Priora?

09:19.610 --> 09:21.110
Who are you?

09:21.110 --> 09:23.280
Huh? My name is Arte.

09:23.950 --> 09:27.090
Uh, we were just having 
a private conversation—

09:27.090 --> 09:28.830
Oh, hey! It's the meat man!

09:28.830 --> 09:31.340
Don't call him that. He's the lord.

09:31.340 --> 09:32.520
Good morning.

09:32.520 --> 09:33.840
Lord!

09:34.470 --> 09:36.340
Meat man!

09:35.270 --> 09:36.590
Hey, that's dangerous.

09:36.340 --> 09:37.690
Lord!

09:52.780 --> 09:54.590
Husband, are you all right?

09:54.590 --> 09:56.120
"Husband"?

09:56.120 --> 09:59.990
I explained to your father 
that we're not engaged.

10:04.550 --> 10:06.710
He just bullied Lada Priora.

10:06.710 --> 10:07.250
Huh?

10:07.820 --> 10:09.230
Uh, wait...

10:08.280 --> 10:09.610
Everyone, rock the boat!

10:09.610 --> 10:10.580
Yay!

10:11.820 --> 10:14.250
I'll give you some meat, so just stop!

10:14.250 --> 10:14.800
Hooray!

10:14.800 --> 10:16.280
This is scary!

10:14.800 --> 10:16.280
Meat, please.

10:16.280 --> 10:19.310
Seriously, stop it!

10:16.280 --> 10:19.310
We love Van!

10:23.760 --> 10:26.270
<i>Scary. Too scary.</i>

10:26.570 --> 10:30.250
Son-in-law. Lada Priora 
told me all about it.

10:30.250 --> 10:34.780
You were flirting with another woman 
when you already have my daughter?

10:35.130 --> 10:37.810
Huh? You mean <i>me</i>?

10:37.810 --> 10:40.340
Well, first of all, I'm not her husband—

10:39.470 --> 10:40.890
We will hold a competition.

10:40.890 --> 10:41.280
Huh?

10:41.550 --> 10:43.490
You will compete against my people,

10:43.490 --> 10:47.950
and if we win, you will officially 
recognize your betrothal to my daughter.

10:48.520 --> 10:49.960
<i>Huh?</i>

10:49.960 --> 10:52.460
We accept your challenge!

10:52.460 --> 10:53.460
Dee?

10:53.460 --> 10:59.090
Leave it to me, the Chivalric Order's 
deputy commander. I'll bring you victory!

10:59.360 --> 11:04.870
Settling this quickly might let you
focus more on your studies, it's true.

11:04.870 --> 11:08.100
Oh? This sounds interesting, Lord Van.

11:08.390 --> 11:10.030
But if I lose—

11:10.030 --> 11:11.180
It's all right.

11:11.900 --> 11:14.360
You'd never lose, Lord Van.

11:14.890 --> 11:17.680
You two are too biased toward me.

11:17.680 --> 11:21.430
Then, shall we settle this 
with a three-round competition?

11:22.030 --> 11:23.370
Very well.

11:23.630 --> 11:26.620
You may choose the nature of 
the first contest, son-in-law.

11:27.030 --> 11:29.300
Hm, what should it be?

11:34.250 --> 11:38.380
So if you land this ball in your 
opponent's zone, you score a point.

11:38.850 --> 11:42.590
I've never seen nor heard
 of such a sport.

11:42.590 --> 11:46.250
Wow, Lord Van. You know something
 even Sir Esparda doesn't.

11:46.250 --> 11:47.640
What incredible knowledge.

11:47.930 --> 11:50.810
<i>I mean, it's just volleyball.</i>

11:51.160 --> 11:55.810
That aside, these swimsuits you made
 for us are very comfortable.

11:54.660 --> 11:55.810
Aw, yeah.

11:56.180 --> 11:59.450
Lady Panamera is what 
every woman aspires to be.

11:59.450 --> 12:01.950
You're joining our side?

12:02.250 --> 12:03.770
Of course.

12:03.770 --> 12:08.140
I need Lord Van to get engaged 
to Lady Arte, after all.

12:08.140 --> 12:10.010
Right, Lady Arte?

12:13.080 --> 12:14.650
Good luck, you two!

12:14.650 --> 12:15.460
You can do it!

12:15.770 --> 12:17.710
Good luck, you two!

12:17.710 --> 12:18.980
Thanks!

12:18.980 --> 12:20.230
Okay. Bring it!

12:31.020 --> 12:33.600
Huh? They might be too good at this.

12:40.450 --> 12:42.610
We're getting crushed.

12:45.580 --> 12:46.940
This is impossible.

12:47.350 --> 12:50.180
Is that the extent of your passion?

12:51.850 --> 12:54.270
If you give up, it's game over.

12:54.900 --> 12:56.600
But the tears spring forth.

12:56.970 --> 12:59.400
I'm a girl, after all.

12:59.880 --> 13:03.130
Fight on!

13:03.370 --> 13:05.380
It's futile! Take this!

13:07.000 --> 13:08.760
I'll make sure to keep it alive!

13:09.670 --> 13:12.140
I'll place everyone's hopes
 into this ball!

13:12.520 --> 13:14.280
And I'll score!

13:19.420 --> 13:21.020
We did it!

13:22.030 --> 13:23.460
Nice smash.

13:23.460 --> 13:25.570
Okay, the real match starts now.

13:25.570 --> 13:26.530
Right!

13:29.720 --> 13:30.740
Here I go!

13:31.950 --> 13:33.080
There!

13:33.080 --> 13:34.090
Weak!

13:34.540 --> 13:36.610
We clawed them back. It's now level.

13:36.610 --> 13:37.910
It's match point.

13:37.910 --> 13:39.790
The next one to score wins.

13:39.790 --> 13:41.350
Have this!

13:41.800 --> 13:42.800
Got it!

13:42.800 --> 13:44.800
This is the end!

13:44.800 --> 13:46.680
I won't let you!

13:54.300 --> 13:55.240
Good.

13:55.240 --> 13:56.430
We won.

14:01.410 --> 14:03.560
We'll have to start over from nothing.

14:03.560 --> 14:04.690
Right.

14:05.000 --> 14:07.750
There's some sports anime
 happening over here.

14:07.750 --> 14:09.200
Now then, son-in-law.

14:09.790 --> 14:12.770
We will decide on the next event.

14:12.770 --> 14:14.900
Sure. What will it be?

14:14.900 --> 14:16.170
Swimming.

14:16.170 --> 14:17.210
Swimming?

14:17.610 --> 14:20.710
The contest will be a two-person relay.

14:20.950 --> 14:25.470
<i>This is bad. If we lose one more event, 
I have to marry Lada Priora.</i>

14:25.470 --> 14:28.010
<i>But the apkallu are master swimmers.</i>

14:28.010 --> 14:29.490
Leave it to me.

14:29.870 --> 14:31.310
Dee? Can you swim?

14:31.310 --> 14:32.650
Of course!

14:32.650 --> 14:34.210
Then, I'll join him.

14:34.210 --> 14:36.350
You, too, Khamsin? Will you be okay?

14:36.350 --> 14:40.350
Yes. I'll give my all for your sake.

14:44.870 --> 14:45.860
Ready.

14:48.370 --> 14:50.690
Ah! She's fast from the very start!

14:51.110 --> 14:53.870
If their lead grows any bigger, 
we're done for.

14:58.570 --> 15:00.870
Khamsin caught up to her!

15:00.870 --> 15:02.880
What tenacity.

15:02.880 --> 15:04.130
You can do it, Khamsin!

15:04.490 --> 15:06.490
Daughter, hurry!

15:10.130 --> 15:11.260
Good.

15:14.520 --> 15:16.010
I'll take it from here.

15:18.770 --> 15:20.020
You did well.

15:20.310 --> 15:22.430
Now, leave it to me!

15:23.110 --> 15:25.080
Why the butterfly stroke?

15:25.080 --> 15:28.290
Sir Dee is at his fastest 
when he swims like that.

15:28.290 --> 15:31.530
That stroke lets him use 
his steel-like muscles to the fullest.

15:33.780 --> 15:36.280
H-How is that man doing that?

15:40.120 --> 15:42.010
We won!

15:43.040 --> 15:44.340
You did it!

15:43.480 --> 15:44.860
You're kidding me.

15:47.150 --> 15:49.550
Isn't that Dee's?

15:49.940 --> 15:52.180
Lord Van, I did it!

15:56.970 --> 16:00.680
I cannot believe we lost at swimming.

16:00.680 --> 16:03.380
However, there is still one event left.

16:03.380 --> 16:06.440
Son-in-law, decide on the final event.

16:07.020 --> 16:08.970
Um...

16:11.540 --> 16:13.080
What is this?

16:13.080 --> 16:15.890
Pluriel, could I ask you 
to produce some ice?

16:15.890 --> 16:16.830
Sure.

16:17.900 --> 16:19.700
Thank you very much.

16:20.430 --> 16:21.530
There we go.

16:26.960 --> 16:28.450
Ta-da.

16:28.960 --> 16:30.580
Whoa.

16:30.580 --> 16:32.590
So, what are we doing with this?

16:32.590 --> 16:35.590
It's a shaved ice speed-eating contest.

16:35.970 --> 16:40.670
We'll compete in teams of two. I'll take
 part this time, so I'll need a teammate.

16:40.670 --> 16:43.650
W-Would it be all right 
for me to participate?

16:48.130 --> 16:49.980
Did I make these too big?

16:49.980 --> 16:54.240
Lady Arte, are you really doing this? 
It's not too late to trade places.

16:54.240 --> 16:56.570
I-I'll be okay.

16:58.700 --> 17:00.170
Then, let's begin.

17:00.170 --> 17:01.240
Ready!

17:07.140 --> 17:08.500
My head...

17:08.500 --> 17:10.530
It stings!

17:12.340 --> 17:15.960
This is for my daughter. 
I can't afford to lose!

17:17.510 --> 17:19.390
Y-Yeah.

17:19.870 --> 17:22.820
W-We might be done for.

17:24.780 --> 17:26.980
Lady Arte! Don't force yourself!

17:33.420 --> 17:35.920
Wow, Lord Van's incredible!

17:35.920 --> 17:37.410
Lady Arte is, too.

17:37.980 --> 17:39.400
We won't lose!

17:39.400 --> 17:40.030
Yeah!

17:51.290 --> 17:52.590
Who will win?

17:54.550 --> 17:56.750
Thank you very much!

17:57.300 --> 17:59.780
Lord Van's team wins!

18:02.220 --> 18:03.270
We lost.

18:03.270 --> 18:04.810
It was a good competition.

18:04.810 --> 18:05.850
Indeed.

18:07.290 --> 18:10.620
Now we can stop all this talk
 of marrying Lada Priora.

18:10.620 --> 18:13.390
I've taken an even greater liking
 to you, son-in-law.

18:14.270 --> 18:17.280
You truly are a man 
worthy of my daughter.

18:17.280 --> 18:20.140
Huh? Then, what was
 the point of winning?

18:20.140 --> 18:22.890
Continue to take good care
 of my daughter.

18:22.890 --> 18:24.590
Farewell, "son-in-law."

18:26.710 --> 18:28.770
No way.

18:29.130 --> 18:30.170
Lord Van?

18:31.500 --> 18:33.020
What's the matter?

18:33.330 --> 18:36.920
M-My stomach hurts from 
eating too much shaved ice.

18:36.920 --> 18:38.300
Oh, my. That's terrible.

18:40.070 --> 18:41.550
You worked hard out there.

18:41.550 --> 18:43.600
I'm glad you won, though.

18:43.600 --> 18:45.380
That was a good competition.

18:45.380 --> 18:47.500
You did well, too, Lady Arte.

18:47.500 --> 18:49.160
Th-Thanks.

18:52.430 --> 18:56.070
<i>Lord Van is always surrounded 
by lots of smiling faces.</i>

18:56.930 --> 19:01.560
<i>How do I get to enjoy that? 
Can I make that happen for me, too?</i>

19:03.730 --> 19:09.030
<i>Since the day I was born, my father was
 always busy, so I barely ever saw him.</i>

19:09.030 --> 19:13.320
<i>My mother handed me off to my wet nurse
 and showed no interest in me.</i>

19:14.040 --> 19:18.610
<i>There was a simple reason
 for that: I was a failure.</i>

19:19.690 --> 19:24.510
<i>I was quite timid and picky,
plus I was no good at studying.</i>

19:25.030 --> 19:27.750
<i>I didn't excel at anything,</i>

19:27.750 --> 19:30.920
<i>save perhaps for my marionette magic.</i>

19:31.970 --> 19:37.610
<i>Using my dolls as puppets, I found I could 
move them more freely than my own body.</i>

19:38.100 --> 19:43.110
<i>So I thought I might be able 
to delight my mother with it.</i>

19:43.620 --> 19:46.050
<i>You bring me such grief!</i>

19:46.870 --> 19:50.920
<i>That was when I first learned
marionette magic is considered evil</i>

19:50.920 --> 19:54.630
<i>and abhorred among the nobility.</i>

19:56.660 --> 20:00.900
<i>After that day, 
no one spoke to me at all,</i>

20:00.900 --> 20:04.090
<i>and I became someone everyone ignored.</i>

20:05.240 --> 20:08.310
<i>Then, when I turned ten,</i>

20:08.310 --> 20:12.250
<i>my father informed me I would 
be getting engaged to someone.</i>

20:12.250 --> 20:14.650
<i>I was filled with anxiety.</i>

20:15.960 --> 20:18.650
<i>But Lord Van was very kind to me.</i>

20:18.650 --> 20:22.490
<i>Then, I learned that Lord Van's aptitude
 wasn't for elemental magic,</i>

20:22.490 --> 20:25.570
<i>but for production magic 
which others considered unfortunate.</i>

20:26.670 --> 20:30.620
<i>Yet Lord Van was brimming 
with confidence and talent,</i>

20:30.970 --> 20:33.340
<i>and he made use of 
his gifts with optimism.</i>

20:33.720 --> 20:38.110
<i>Perhaps if I hadn't stopped 
practicing my magic after that day...</i>

20:40.120 --> 20:43.480
<i>I think I'm going to try
 a little harder, too.</i>

20:45.570 --> 20:49.930
We'll build more ramparts with an eye
toward the village's future development.

20:49.930 --> 20:53.740
Please take the utmost care 
to work safely and avoid injuries.

20:53.740 --> 20:54.880
Yes, sir.

20:54.880 --> 20:56.940
By the way, since tomorrow's a day off,

20:56.940 --> 21:00.050
we'll be hosting a big barbecue tonight.

21:00.440 --> 21:02.690
Let's all work hard until then.

21:02.690 --> 21:04.700
Yeah!

21:05.350 --> 21:07.060
All right!

21:05.960 --> 21:07.560
Let's do this!

21:07.560 --> 21:09.030
Barbecue!

21:07.910 --> 21:10.230
That was an interesting way
 to motivate them.

21:10.630 --> 21:14.290
Sorry that it's kind of lax. 
It's always like this.

21:14.290 --> 21:15.350
Lord Van.

21:16.410 --> 21:18.960
G-Good morning.

21:19.450 --> 21:21.930
Good morning, Lady Arte.

21:21.930 --> 21:27.240
I-It looks like we'll have 
good weather all day today.

21:27.770 --> 21:31.220
Did something happen? You seem 
more energetic than usual today.

21:31.550 --> 21:35.690
Y-Yes. I'm feeling 
very energetic today. So...

21:37.560 --> 21:38.980
What is it?

21:39.940 --> 21:41.860
<i>Even if it's just a tiny glimpse,</i>

21:41.860 --> 21:45.430
<i>I want to see things
the way Lord Van sees them.</i>

21:45.430 --> 21:47.180
<i>I want to get closer to that.</i>

21:48.440 --> 21:52.510
Would it be all right
 if I watched you work?

21:53.700 --> 21:55.500
Yes, of course.

22:02.970 --> 22:04.060
Boss!

